PEG morphologystatus of

A word on authority: this grammar descends from the language-definition committee's formal morphology effort. It is a de facto standard – a working document that was never put to a ratifying vote, but is implemented by the current Lojban software tools surveyed for this edition. One rule within it, the ban on consonant-glide-vowel sequences, was separately adopted by a recorded committee vote in December 2014 (see
). The text below is taken verbatim from the grammar used by the camxes parser family, at the revision pinned for this edition's verification work.
